===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=main|:inh|enm:all}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂el-|id=all}}
From {{inh|en|enm|all}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eall}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*all}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*allaz}}, of uncertain origin<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref> but perhaps from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂el-|id=all|t=all}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|a}}, {{m|sco|a'}}, {{m|sco|aa}}, {{m|sco|aal}}, {{m|sco|aw|t=all}}, {{cog|yol|aal}}, {{m|yol|al}}, {{m|yol|all}}, {{m|yol|aul|t=all}}, {{cog|frr|aal}}, {{m|frr|aale}}, {{m|frr|ale}}, {{m|frr|ali}}, {{m|frr|åle|t=all}}, {{cog|stq|al|t=already}}, {{m|stq|aal|t=all}}, {{cog|fy|alle|t=all}}, {{cog|nl|al|t=all}}, {{cog|de,lb|all|t=all}}, {{cog|wym|oły}}, {{m|wym|ołły|t=all}}, {{cog|yi|אַלע|t=all}}, {{cog|da|al|t=all}}, {{cog|fo,is|allur|t=all}}, {{cog|nb,sv|all|t=all}}, {{cog|nn|aillj}}, {{m|nn|all|t=all}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌻𐌻𐍃|t=all}}; also {{cog|br,cy|holl|t=all}}, {{cog|kw|oll|t=all}}, {{cog|ga|alig}}, {{m|ga|eile}}, {{m|ga|uile}}, {{m|ga|uileag}}, {{m|ga|uilig|t=all}}, {{cog|gv|ooilley|t=all}}, {{cog|gd|uile}}, {{m|gd|uileag|t=all}}, {{cog|lt|aliái|t=every}}, {{cog|hy|ողջ|t=entire, whole}}.
{{col-bottom}}
The dialectal sense “all gone” is a {{cal|en|de|alle|nocap=1}}. The use in {{m|en||who all, where all}} etc. also has equivalents in German (see {{m|de|alles}}).

